Reason: in a GameMaker 1 room the draw list is the instances merged into the room's tiles, and every rebuild of it (any
instance created or destroyed: most frames in rm_a3h04, with ~750 instances and ~4,800 tiles) placed each instance by
binary search over the tiles before writing the tiles out, and then the tile-skip map and the draw events walked the
whole list once more: on the console ~1.9 ms of rebuild plus ~0.7 ms of walks a frame. A tile sorts before an
instance or particle system exactly when its depth is at least theirs, so one pass over the tile run writes the tiles
and puts each other entry in as soon as the next tile is below its depth; the instances sort on keys worked out once;
and the pass keeps the positions of the entries that are not tiles, from which the tile-skip query and the draw events
find their places. The list is the same.
Upstream: Speed only, every platform. Retires this patch when merged.

